// ============================================================================
// SCORE SCREEN
// ============================================================================
//
// Shown after the reward summary, as the last thing the player reads. The order
// matters: rewards answer "what did I get", the score answers "how well did I
// play", and only the second one is worth staring at before restarting.
//
// The screen itself is pure presentation — every number and every line of art
// comes from engine/score.lor, so a new tier or a new component never touches
// this file.

// THE GATE. The record is reached on purpose, never by scrolling into it.
//
// Without this single-option choice the panel arrived in the same breath as the
// reward summary, and the rank flashed past while the player was still reading
// how much XP they earned. A deliberate click separates the two questions —
// what the battle paid, then how it was won — and gives the verdict a screen of
// its own.
beat ScoreScreen
  choice
    View the battle record
      -> ScoreCard


beat ScoreCard
  $scoreScreen()

  choice
    Restart menu
      -> Start

    End
      -> .
